{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceFormSemisimple","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TraceFormSemisimple","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceNilpotent","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Artinian.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Artinian.Module","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Jacobson.Ideal"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceForm_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceForm_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceFormSemisimple.lean#L50-L77","doc":"**Abstract semisimplicity from a nondegenerate regular trace form\n(sorry-free).**  A finite-dimensional `K`-algebra whose regular trace\nform is nondegenerate is a semisimple ring.  This is the general\nengine behind Wenzl's / Geck–Pfeiffer's criterion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceForm_comm","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TraceFormSemisimple.lean#L42-L48","doc":"**The regular trace form is symmetric/cyclic (sorry-free).**\n`B(x, y) = trace(L_x L_y) = trace(L_y L_x) = B(y, x)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}